---
description: CI, Docker, and Docker Compose VM deployment rules
globs: .github/**/*,Dockerfile*,infrastructure/**/*,docker-compose*.yml,scripts/*deploy*,docs/DEPLOYMENT.md,docs/BACKUP_ROLLBACK.md
alwaysApply: false
---

# DevOps / deploy

- Production is a Docker Compose stack on the VM, deployed from `main` with `scripts/vm-selective-redeploy.py` (fresh VM / full rebuild: `scripts/remote-deploy.py`)—see `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`.
- Production deploys only with explicit human approval.
- Always include rollback notes (`docs/BACKUP_ROLLBACK.md`) in deploy-related changes.
- Never weaken `security.yml` checks without an explicit human decision recorded in the PR.
